    "body": "I added another item, \"Queued calls to writer methods such as write() are not cancelled when writer.releaseLock() is called. This makes them easy to use in a \"fire and forget\" style.\" which raises the question of exactly how much detail belongs in this section.\r\n\r\nPersonally I'm happy with it being quite inclusive, but I don't think it should be an exhaustive list of every design decision we ever made.\r\n\r\nMaybe I should rephrase it as \"Fire-and-forget style usage is supported. Therefore...\"",
